# What each motion is for
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.ui.button.lift=A glyph button under the pointer: it dips, rises a pixel past its mark and settles; pressed it drops onto the surface; let go it springs back in three shrinking lobes; left it returns quicker than it rose.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.ui.button.turn=The lift with a turn, for a glyph big and lopsided enough to show one: it turns while it travels and is square wherever it rests.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.ui.button.snap=The lift further and quicker, for a decisive control such as a cross, which answers like a switch.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.ui.button.lit=A control crossing to its lit artwork and back: most of the way in this many seconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.ui.tip.show=A tip beside the pointer fading in the moment the pointer reaches something. For 'warm' milliseconds after a tip went, the next one stands whole at once.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.bar.appear=The input bars' own entrance, up from below with a small swing as they land. At 0 milliseconds they have none and arrive with their window; given a time, they come up on their own instead.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.sub.open=A sub-window opening where it stands, rising its last pixels into place, and fading out there as it closes.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.tab.move=A tab gliding to its place and width in the row.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.tab.controls=A tab's own controls going and coming as the row narrows and widens: the room glides in one half, the ink fades in the other.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.tab.lift=A carried tab rising its pixel off the row, and settling back once it is put down.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.tab.glow=The glow a tab put down gives once in its colour, on its own surface and the tool strip's, fading out in this many milliseconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.tab.marquee=A name cut short read whole under a resting pointer: after this many milliseconds it slides speed pixels a second until its end shows, rests pause milliseconds there, slides back, and rests again.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.snap.assist=The snap assist's panes coming and going.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.snap.layouts=The snap layouts' flyout coming and going, and the snap bar coming all the way down from its peek once the pointer touches it, and back.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.snap.preview=The frosted preview of where a window will snap, growing out of the window and fading.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.snap.bar.peek=The snap bar peeking further down from the top of the screen as a carried window's pointer comes nearer it, and back up: most of the way in this many seconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.search.clear=The search well's magnifier crossing over to its cross while a search stands in it.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.fill=A window gliding to the part of the screen it fills, and back.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.appear=A new window fading in.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.icon.flip=A chevron control playing its run of frames between open and closed.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.scroll=A history, list or panel gliding to where it was scrolled: most of the way in this many seconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.hover.fade=A row or control crossing to its lit shade and back.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.stack.fade=A window or a sub-window fading an eighth for each window that comes to lie over it, down to half, and back as they go: most of the way in this many seconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.marquee.return=A name cut short gliding home once the pointer leaves it.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.notice=A short notice over a window's bar, why a page closed by itself or that a locked window cannot be changed: fading in as it rises its last pixels, standing hold milliseconds while it is read, then fading out where it stands.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.answer=A page's answer over its bar, saved or refused: fading in as it rises its last pixels, standing hold milliseconds while it is read, then fading out where it stands. One that waits for the server stands until the answer comes.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.view.line=Exit Borderless (Esc), at the top of a borderless window: fading in, standing hold milliseconds as the page comes to fill it and while the pointer is near the top, then fading out where it stands.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.window.bar.grow=An input bar growing a row taller as the words typed in it wrap onto another row, and shrinking back: most of the way in this many seconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.line.hover=A chat line under the pointer. The chevron lights toward a lighter shade of its speaker's colour, then steps a pixel right; the words follow three pixels as one block. A stagger on the words' on beat sends them one after another instead, spread over stagger_span, and a gap bump stretches the row by its gaps while they travel (gap: pixels across the row). Leaving is quicker: the words go back first and the chevron follows.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.line.appear=The newest message: the stack rises into place while the line slides in from the side, past its place and back, fading in a little ahead of the motion.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.row.move=A row of the history gliding to its place when the lines are laid out again.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.row.appear=A row new to the history's layout fading in where it lands.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.window.area=A window's timestamp area driven out and back in.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.window.members=A window's member list coming out and going back in.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.jump.show=The jump-to-present button flying in while a history is scrolled back, and out again.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.toolbar.show=A message's toolbar coming up after a scroll: it stays away while the history moves, waits until the pointer has rested on one message for 'rest' milliseconds, then fades in. The rest is the pointer's, so the Animations settings leave it as it is.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.feed.typing=The chat feed's lines rising a row for its typing row, and settling back.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.chat.scrollbar.fade=The scrollbar coming and going.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.open=A screen's content arriving as it opens: from start_x and start_y pixels off its place and start_scale of its size, into place. The chat's windows open on it too.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.backdrop=The veil and blur behind a screen fading in.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.control_bar=A screen's bottom control strip's own entrance: waiting delay milliseconds, then rising travel pixels into place. At 0 milliseconds it has none and arrives with its screen's content; given a time, it comes up on its own instead.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.journal.fold=The quest journal's categories folding and unfolding, and its search field growing out of the magnifier.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.journal.scroll=The quest journal's lists and its reading marker gliding to where they were scrolled.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.characters.glide=The Characters tab's roster and profile gliding to where they were scrolled, and its figure to the zoom the wheel gave it.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.screen.dialogue.glide=A quest conversation's replies gliding to bring the chosen one to the middle.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.hud.chat.hide=The HUD fading out as one layer while the chat is open, and back in once it closes.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.hud.feed.rise=The chat feed at its default place following the rows over the hotbar up and down as hearts, armour or air come and go: most of the way in this many seconds.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.inventory.item.slide=An item stack sliding from one slot to another.
gui.losttales.motionlab.about.map.popup.open=A popup on the map coming up: from travel pixels below and start_scale of its size, into place.
gui.losttales.motionlab.pick=Pick a motion from the list.
