#   Config: each category's and each option's name and tip, and the words a server
#   option of a few words takes (losttales.config.<category>.<key>, .tooltip, .<word>).
#   The game shows them in each player's language; the English tips are the comments
#   of the files under config/losttales/.
#   client, in client/client.cfg
losttales.config.category.client=Client / HUD
losttales.config.category.client.tooltip=HUD visibility, placement, compass, fellowship, quick-loot, quest tracker, and client feedback options.
losttales.config.client.animations=Animations
losttales.config.client.animations.tooltip=Let the mod's screens, HUD and chat move. Off, everything stands where it ends. How each motion looks is in the motion files (assets/losttales/motion, tuned in the Motion Lab).
losttales.config.client.animationSpeed=Speed
losttales.config.client.animationSpeed.tooltip=How fast every motion plays: 2 is twice as fast, 0.5 half as fast.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedAlignment=Alignment
losttales.config.client.chatFeedAlignment.tooltip=Which edge the chat feed's lines stand against: LEFT, CENTRE (the default), or RIGHT. Each line's background thins out away from that edge, from the middle to both sides for CENTRE.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedLines=Lines
losttales.config.client.chatFeedLines.tooltip=The most lines the chat feed shows at once; never more than half the screen holds. Set in a conversation's Chat Feed Settings.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedMessageSize=Message Size
losttales.config.client.chatFeedMessageSize.tooltip=How big what a message says is in the chat feed, against the same words in the open window: SMALLER, SAME or LARGER. The open window's words are the size every other row is measured against and are set by the game's Chat Scale.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedQuoteSize=Reply Quote Size
losttales.config.client.chatFeedQuoteSize.tooltip=The same row in the chat feed, against the feed's own words: SMALLER, SAME or LARGER. SAME, the default, draws the quote as large as the words it stands over.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedSeconds=Seconds on Screen
losttales.config.client.chatFeedSeconds.tooltip=How many seconds a line stays in the chat feed, fading in the last of them. Set in a conversation's Chat Feed Settings.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedSpeakerSize=Speaker Name Size
losttales.config.client.chatFeedSpeakerSize.tooltip=The same row in the chat feed, against the feed's own words: SMALLER, SAME or LARGER. LARGER, the default, stands it a step over them, which is the size the open window's words have, so a glance reads the voices first.
losttales.config.client.chatFeedWidth=Width
losttales.config.client.chatFeedWidth.tooltip=How wide the chat feed stands, in GUI pixels. Set in a conversation's Chat Feed Settings.
losttales.config.client.chatHistoryLines=Messages Kept
losttales.config.client.chatHistoryLines.tooltip=Chat messages kept in the history, shared by every channel tab (vanilla keeps 100).
losttales.config.client.chatMentionLineColor=Mention Colour
losttales.config.client.chatMentionLineColor.tooltip=Palette colour of a chat line that @-mentions you. Set in Settings.
losttales.config.client.chatPingSound=Ping Sound
losttales.config.client.chatPingSound.tooltip=Sound event played when a chat message @-mentions you; empty disables the sound.
losttales.config.client.chatProfanityFilter=Profanity Filter
losttales.config.client.chatProfanityFilter.tooltip=How the words on the chat's profanity list read on this client: OFF as typed, SILLY as their silly stand-ins (fuck reads flip, shit reads poop), STARS as their first letter and stars (f***). Display only: what you type reaches everyone else as typed, and what they see is their own setting's. The list is the mod's, plus the server's words and any in client/chat/profanity.txt.
losttales.config.client.chatQuoteSize=Reply Quote Size
losttales.config.client.chatQuoteSize.tooltip=How big the row a reply opens with is in the open chat window, the quote of the message it answers, against the words under it: SMALLER, SAME or LARGER.
losttales.config.client.chatReplyHighlightColor=Reply Highlight Colour
losttales.config.client.chatReplyHighlightColor.tooltip=Palette colour a chat line is lit in when a reply's quote jumps to it. Set in Settings.
losttales.config.client.chatSelectedMentionColor=Selected Mention Colour
losttales.config.client.chatSelectedMentionColor.tooltip=Palette colour of a chat line that @-mentions you while it is under the pointer. AUTO, the default, is the mention colour one shade lighter on its own ramp of the palette, or the windows' secondary colour where the mention colour is already its ramp's lightest. Set in Settings.
losttales.config.client.chatSpeakerSize=Speaker Name Size
losttales.config.client.chatSpeakerSize.tooltip=How big the row a message names its speaker on is in the open chat window, against the words under it: SMALLER, SAME or LARGER, each one whole display pixel per font pixel, which is the only step that keeps the font crisp. The row is as tall as the text it is drawn in.
losttales.config.client.chestBounce=Chest Bounce
losttales.config.client.chestBounce.tooltip=Strength of the chest physics; 0 is still, 1 is the most movement.
losttales.config.client.chestPhysics=Chest Physics
losttales.config.client.chestPhysics.tooltip=Let the chest sway and bounce with movement.
losttales.config.client.closeMapTerrainTransitionEndZoom=Fade Ends at Zoom
losttales.config.client.closeMapTerrainTransitionEndZoom.tooltip=Zoom exponent where prepared close-map terrain may fully replace the ordinary LOTR map. Must be greater than closeMapTerrainTransitionStartZoom.
losttales.config.client.closeMapTerrainTransitionStartZoom=Fade Starts at Zoom
losttales.config.client.closeMapTerrainTransitionStartZoom.tooltip=Zoom exponent where the close-map terrain transition begins. The ordinary LOTR map remains fully visible at and below this value.
losttales.config.client.compassHudDisplayRadius=Field of View (Degrees)
losttales.config.client.compassHudDisplayRadius.tooltip=Visible compass field in degrees. Larger values show more markers but reduce precision.
losttales.config.client.compassHudOffsetX=Compass Across the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.compassHudOffsetX.tooltip=Horizontal compass position as a percentage of the scaled screen width.
losttales.config.client.compassHudOffsetY=Compass Down the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.compassHudOffsetY.tooltip=Vertical compass position as a percentage of the scaled screen height.
losttales.config.client.convertChatEmoticons=Turn Emoticons into Emoji
losttales.config.client.convertChatEmoticons.tooltip=Turn classic emoticons you type (:) :D <3 ...) into their emojis as the message is sent.
losttales.config.client.customWaypointColors=Custom Waypoint Colours
losttales.config.client.customWaypointColors.tooltip=Client-only icon colour per custom waypoint, as name=colour. LOTR stores no colour for its waypoints, so this is presentation only and is not shared with anyone else.
losttales.config.client.customWaypointNotes=Custom Waypoint Notes
losttales.config.client.customWaypointNotes.tooltip=Client-only tooltip note per custom waypoint, as name=note. LOTR stores no description for its waypoints, so this is presentation only and is not shared with anyone else.
losttales.config.client.devSkinOverrideBodyType=Override Arms
losttales.config.client.devSkinOverrideBodyType.tooltip=Arm width for the override skin: wide or slim. Anything else means wide.
losttales.config.client.devSkinOverridePath=Skin Override File
losttales.config.client.devSkinOverridePath.tooltip=Developer aid: path of a 64x32 or 64x64 PNG drawn on your own player instead of your account skin. Empty disables it.
losttales.config.client.enableChatEmojis=Emoji
losttales.config.client.enableChatEmojis.tooltip=Render supported :shortcodes: as inline emojis and show the chat emoji picker.
losttales.config.client.enableChatMessageGrouping=Group Messages
losttales.config.client.enableChatMessageGrouping.tooltip=Drop the repeated head and name when the same identity sends several messages in a row.
losttales.config.client.enableChatPings=Pings
losttales.config.client.enableChatPings.tooltip=Highlight and play a sound for chat messages that @-mention your account or active character name.
losttales.config.client.enableGuiBackground=Darken Behind Screens
losttales.config.client.enableGuiBackground.tooltip=Draw the dark semi-transparent background behind compatible GUIs.
losttales.config.client.enableGuiBackgroundBlur=Blur Behind Screens
losttales.config.client.enableGuiBackgroundBlur.tooltip=Blur the world behind compatible GUIs when legacy framebuffer shaders are available.
losttales.config.client.enableNpcChatStyling=NPC Speech in the Chat's Style
losttales.config.client.enableNpcChatStyling.tooltip=Show LOTR NPC speech through the Lost Tales chat style with head icons, timestamps, and channels.
losttales.config.client.enableQuestDialogue=Quest Conversations
losttales.config.client.enableQuestDialogue.tooltip=Talk to a quest giver in the Lost Tales conversation screen. Off, Middle-earth quests are offered on LOTR's own screen, and a Lost Tales quest giver's words go to the chat while their quest is taken or handed in on touch.
losttales.config.client.fellowshipCompassMarkerFadeRadius=Fellowship Fade Distance (Blocks)
losttales.config.client.fellowshipCompassMarkerFadeRadius.tooltip=Distance in blocks over which fellowship-member compass markers fade to their minimum opacity. Beyond this distance they remain visible at the opacity floor.
losttales.config.client.fellowshipHudOffsetX=Fellowship Across the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.fellowshipHudOffsetX.tooltip=Horizontal fellowship HUD position as a percentage of the scaled screen width.
losttales.config.client.fellowshipHudOffsetY=Fellowship Down the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.fellowshipHudOffsetY.tooltip=Vertical fellowship HUD position as a percentage of the scaled screen height.
losttales.config.client.guiAlwaysBlur=Blur Behind Every Screen
losttales.config.client.guiAlwaysBlur.tooltip=Blur every compatible in-world GUI background, including screens that opt out by default.
losttales.config.client.guiBackgroundOpacity=Darkness
losttales.config.client.guiBackgroundOpacity.tooltip=Final opacity of the GUI's black background veil.
losttales.config.client.guiBlurStrength=Blur Strength
losttales.config.client.guiBlurStrength.tooltip=Background blur radius. Blur failure falls back to the normal GUI background.
losttales.config.client.hiddenMapLegendCategories=Hidden Map Legend Categories
losttales.config.client.hiddenMapLegendCategories.tooltip=Client-only map legend category IDs that are hidden. Unknown IDs are ignored and new categories remain visible by default.
losttales.config.client.hideHudWithWindows=Hide the HUD While Windows Are Open
losttales.config.client.hideHudWithWindows.tooltip=Fade the game's HUD (hotbar, health, crosshair and the rest) and the Lost Tales panels out while the window screen is open, and back in when it closes.
losttales.config.client.hostileCompassMarkerScanRadius=Enemy Range (Blocks)
losttales.config.client.hostileCompassMarkerScanRadius.tooltip=Client display radius in blocks for enemy compass markers. The server tracking radius remains authoritative.
losttales.config.client.hostileMapMarkerDisplayRadius=Enemy Range (Blocks)
losttales.config.client.hostileMapMarkerDisplayRadius.tooltip=Client display radius in blocks for transient enemy markers on the LOTR main map. The server tracking radius remains authoritative.
losttales.config.client.hudPlacementPreset=HUD Panel Layout
losttales.config.client.hudPlacementPreset.tooltip=Where the HUD's panels stand: custom keeps each panel where it was placed; default, lotr-safe, compact and minimal put every panel in that layout's place. Set in Client Settings, HUD.
losttales.config.client.linkShowCompassHud=Compass Shown and Hidden with the HUD
losttales.config.client.linkShowCompassHud.tooltip=When true, changing showLostTalesHud also changes showCompassHud. Disabled by default in the 1.7.10 backport to preserve existing per-HUD settings.
losttales.config.client.linkShowFellowshipHud=Fellowship Shown and Hidden with the HUD
losttales.config.client.linkShowFellowshipHud.tooltip=When true, changing showLostTalesHud also changes showFellowshipHud.
losttales.config.client.linkShowQuestHud=Quest Tracker Shown and Hidden with the HUD
losttales.config.client.linkShowQuestHud.tooltip=When true, changing showLostTalesHud also changes showQuestHud. Off, the quest tracker keeps its own setting.
losttales.config.client.linkShowQuickLootHud=Quick Loot Shown and Hidden with the HUD
losttales.config.client.linkShowQuickLootHud.tooltip=When true, changing showLostTalesHud also changes showQuickLootHud. Disabled by default in the 1.7.10 backport to preserve existing per-HUD settings.
losttales.config.client.notificationHudOffsetX=Notifications Across the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.notificationHudOffsetX.tooltip=Horizontal position of the notification slot (quest banners, location discoveries, area names) within the available scaled screen width.
losttales.config.client.notificationHudOffsetY=Notifications Down the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.notificationHudOffsetY.tooltip=Vertical position of the notification slot within the available scaled screen height.
losttales.config.client.npcConversationsOpen=NPC Conversations Open
losttales.config.client.npcConversationsOpen.tooltip=How many conversations with NPCs open a page by themselves; older ones wait in +.
losttales.config.client.onlyShowUnlockedLotrWaypoints=Only Unlocked Waypoints
losttales.config.client.onlyShowUnlockedLotrWaypoints.tooltip=Only show LOTR waypoints on the compass after the player has unlocked them according to LOTR's own waypoint logic.
losttales.config.client.pinnedWindowOpacity=Pinned Window Opacity
losttales.config.client.pinnedWindowOpacity.tooltip=How strong a pinned window shows while you play, in percent of how it shows on the window screen.
losttales.config.client.playQuestSounds=Quest Sounds
losttales.config.client.playQuestSounds.tooltip=Play simple vanilla UI sounds for quest milestones.
losttales.config.client.questHudMaxTrackedQuests=Tracked Quests Shown
losttales.config.client.questHudMaxTrackedQuests.tooltip=Maximum number of tracked quests drawn on the quest HUD before showing an overflow count.
losttales.config.client.questHudObjectiveLineCount=Objective Lines per Quest
losttales.config.client.questHudObjectiveLineCount.tooltip=The most text lines a tracked quest's objectives take on the tracker, all its objectives together.
losttales.config.client.questHudOffsetX=Quest Tracker Across the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.questHudOffsetX.tooltip=Horizontal quest tracker position as a percentage of the scaled screen width.
losttales.config.client.questHudOffsetY=Quest Tracker Down the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.questHudOffsetY.tooltip=Vertical quest tracker position as a percentage of the scaled screen height.
losttales.config.client.quickLootHudMaxRows=Most Rows
losttales.config.client.quickLootHudMaxRows.tooltip=Maximum number of item rows visible in the Quick Loot HUD.
losttales.config.client.quickLootHudOffsetX=Quick Loot Across the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.quickLootHudOffsetX.tooltip=Horizontal quick-loot position as a percentage of the scaled screen width.
losttales.config.client.quickLootHudOffsetY=Quick Loot Down the Screen (%)
losttales.config.client.quickLootHudOffsetY.tooltip=Vertical quick-loot position as a percentage of the scaled screen height.
losttales.config.client.reducedMotion=Reduced Motion
losttales.config.client.reducedMotion.tooltip=Keep motion to short fades: nothing travels, overshoots, anticipates or stretches.
losttales.config.client.sendChatTypingStatus=Show Others That I Am Typing
losttales.config.client.sendChatTypingStatus.tooltip=Let the people who would read your message see that you are typing it.
losttales.config.client.showChatSpeechBubbles=Speech Bubbles
losttales.config.client.showChatSpeechBubbles.tooltip=Show what a player says in character over their head, the way LOTR shows an NPC's speech, as far as the server's Proximity radius. In-character channels only (Global, Proximity, Fellowship, Faction and whispers); never OOC, the operator channel, the Console or the Server Log.
losttales.config.client.showChatTypingIndicators=Show Who Is Typing
losttales.config.client.showChatTypingIndicators.tooltip=Show who is typing into a channel above that window's input bar.
losttales.config.client.showCompassHud=Compass Panel
losttales.config.client.showCompassHud.tooltip=Render the Lost Tales compass HUD.
losttales.config.client.showDiscoveredWorldMapMarkers=Other Found Markers
losttales.config.client.showDiscoveredWorldMapMarkers.tooltip=Also render world-space labels for discovered non-quest map markers. Disable this if too many map markers clutter the world view.
losttales.config.client.showFellowshipHud=Fellowship Panel
losttales.config.client.showFellowshipHud.tooltip=Render the compact fellowship member HUD while the active role-playing character belongs to a fellowship.
losttales.config.client.showHostileCompassMarkers=Enemies in Combat
losttales.config.client.showHostileCompassMarkers.tooltip=Render server-approved enemies actively engaged with the local player on the Lost Tales compass.
losttales.config.client.showHostileMapMarkers=Enemies in Combat
losttales.config.client.showHostileMapMarkers.tooltip=Render transient active-combat enemy markers on the LOTR main map. These markers are never saved.
losttales.config.client.showLostTalesHud=Lost Tales HUD
losttales.config.client.showLostTalesHud.tooltip=Master toggle for Lost Tales HUD elements.
losttales.config.client.showLotrWaypointCompassMarkers=LOTR Waypoints
losttales.config.client.showLotrWaypointCompassMarkers.tooltip=Render public Lord of the Rings Legacy waypoints as compass Point of Interest markers.
losttales.config.client.showNativeLotrQuestTracker=LOTR's Quest Tracker
losttales.config.client.showNativeLotrQuestTracker.tooltip=Also render LOTR's original single-quest tracker as a compatibility fallback.
losttales.config.client.showQuestChatFeedback=Quest Lines in the Chat
losttales.config.client.showQuestChatFeedback.tooltip=Show the server's quest notes in the Console: tracking, markers found and rewards received. Off hides only these notes; a refusal always shows.
losttales.config.client.showQuestHud=Quest Tracker Panel
losttales.config.client.showQuestHud.tooltip=Render the Lost Tales active quest tracker and quest notifications.
losttales.config.client.showQuestHudNotifications=Quest Banners
losttales.config.client.showQuestHudNotifications.tooltip=Render centered quest notification banners for quest starts, objective progress, and completions.
losttales.config.client.showQuickLootHud=Quick Loot Panel
losttales.config.client.showQuickLootHud.tooltip=Render the Quick Loot HUD when looking at supported inventories.
losttales.config.client.showSkinOverlays=Skin Overlays
losttales.config.client.showSkinOverlays.tooltip=Draw the jacket, sleeve, and trouser overlay layers of 64x64 skins on players.
losttales.config.client.showStaticCompassMarkers=Map Markers
losttales.config.client.showStaticCompassMarkers.tooltip=Render JSON-defined/static map markers on the compass.
losttales.config.client.showWorldQuestMarkers=Quest Markers
losttales.config.client.showWorldQuestMarkers.tooltip=Show labels in the world over the places tracked quests send you: the quest's title and how far it is.
losttales.config.client.windowBackgroundBlur=Blur the World Behind Windows
losttales.config.client.windowBackgroundBlur.tooltip=Blur the world inside each window's box while the window screen is open; the rest of the screen stays sharp. Needs enableGuiBackgroundBlur.
losttales.config.client.windowPrimaryColor=Primary Colour
losttales.config.client.windowPrimaryColor.tooltip=Palette colour of every window's and sub-window's surface: the content, the member list, menus, cards and tips. Set in Settings.
losttales.config.client.windowSecondaryColor=Secondary Colour
losttales.config.client.windowSecondaryColor.tooltip=Palette colour of every window's strips and bars: the tool strip, the input bar, a sub-window's strip, the tab in front, hairlines and every lit row, the chat line under the pointer among them. Set in Settings.
losttales.config.client.windowAccentColor=Accent Colour
losttales.config.client.windowAccentColor.tooltip=Palette colour of what lights up and leads the eye in every window: lit buttons and glyphs, the fade where a list goes on, the line two windows line up on, and what the Server and the Client say in the chat. Set in Settings.
losttales.config.client.worldQuestMarkerMaxDistance=Farthest Shown (Blocks)
losttales.config.client.worldQuestMarkerMaxDistance.tooltip=Quest marker labels in the world show out to this many blocks.
#   third_person_camera, in client/third-person.cfg
losttales.config.category.client.thirdPersonCamera=Third-Person Camera
losttales.config.category.client.thirdPersonCamera.tooltip=Optional modern rear camera, profile transitions, shoulder framing, FOV response, collision safety, and editable presets from config/losttales/camera_presets.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.aimingBodyRotationSpeed=Turn Speed Aiming
losttales.config.third_person_camera.aimingBodyRotationSpeed.tooltip=Body turn speed in degrees per second while holding or using a direction-sensitive item.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.airborneMotionMultiplier=Jumping and Falling
losttales.config.third_person_camera.airborneMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales the restrained vertical camera lag while jumping or falling. Zero disables airborne motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.attackBodyRotationSpeed=Turn Speed Attacking
losttales.config.third_person_camera.attackBodyRotationSpeed.tooltip=Maximum visual body turn speed during and immediately after an attack.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.attackCommitmentSeconds=Attack Commitment (Seconds)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.attackCommitmentSeconds.tooltip=How long a melee swing visually commits the body to its attack direction. This never blocks or changes server movement input.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.attackMotionMultiplier=Attacking
losttales.config.third_person_camera.attackMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales the small forward camera impulse at the beginning of a player attack. Zero disables attack motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.bodyRotationSpeed=Turn Speed
losttales.config.third_person_camera.bodyRotationSpeed.tooltip=Normal body turn speed in degrees per second.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.cameraMotionMultiplier=Strength
losttales.config.third_person_camera.cameraMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Master scale for all follow, locomotion, idle, and situational camera translation. Zero disables camera motion while retaining profile framing transitions.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.cameraPreset=Preset
losttales.config.third_person_camera.cameraPreset.tooltip=Base camera framing preset loaded from config/losttales/camera_presets. The multipliers below fine-tune the selected preset.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.cameraPreset.modern_action_rpg=Modern Action RPG
losttales.config.third_person_camera.collisionPadding=Room Kept from Walls (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.collisionPadding.tooltip=Camera collision padding in blocks. Larger values keep the view farther from surfaces.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.collisionReleaseRate=Return After a Wall
losttales.config.third_person_camera.collisionReleaseRate.tooltip=How quickly the camera moves back out after an obstruction clears.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.combatProfileHoldSeconds=Combat Camera Stays (Seconds)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.combatProfileHoldSeconds.tooltip=How long the combat camera remains after attacking, aiming, or taking damage.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.combatProfileWithWeaponHeld=Combat Camera with a Weapon
losttales.config.third_person_camera.combatProfileWithWeaponHeld.tooltip=Use the combat camera while a recognized vanilla, Lost Tales, or LOTR weapon is held.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.damageMotionMultiplier=Taking Damage
losttales.config.third_person_camera.damageMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales the short camera reaction when the player takes damage. Zero disables damage motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.defaultRightShoulder=Start Over the Right Shoulder
losttales.config.third_person_camera.defaultRightShoulder.tooltip=Start each world/session over the player's right shoulder.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.distanceMultiplier=Distance
losttales.config.third_person_camera.distanceMultiplier.tooltip=Multiplier for every profile's camera distance.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableCameraIntentTargeting=Aim from the Camera
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableCameraIntentTargeting.tooltip=Aim from the camera center, then validate the result from the player's eye using vanilla reach and line of sight. Disable this compatibility fallback to retain vanilla eye-forward targeting.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableCameraMotion=Camera Motion
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableCameraMotion.tooltip=Enable bounded world-follow motion, stride and idle sway, and the situational airborne, riding, swimming, combat, damage, and explosion effects below. Target validation and the fixed crosshair remain stable.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableChargeTierFeedback=Charge Feedback
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableChargeTierFeedback.tooltip=Show client feedback for charge tiers confirmed by the server.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableChargeTierParticles=Charge Particles
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableChargeTierParticles.tooltip=Show restrained vanilla particle effects when ranged charge tiers activate and release.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableChargeTierSounds=Charge Sounds
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableChargeTierSounds.tooltip=Play short vanilla sound cues when ranged charge tiers activate and release.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enabled=Third-Person Camera
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enabled.tooltip=Enable the Lost Tales third-person overhaul. F5 uses only first and rear third person while enabled; disabling the overhaul restores vanilla's front-facing F5 view.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableDirectionalMovement=Turn the Body to Movement
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableDirectionalMovement.tooltip=Turn the locally rendered player body toward camera-relative movement while keeping vanilla look, targeting, and network direction authoritative.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableFovEffects=Field of View Effects
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableFovEffects.tooltip=Apply the restrained movement-profile FOV offsets.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableProjectileAimCorrection=Aim Correction
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableProjectileAimCorrection.tooltip=Align supported vanilla and LOTR projectiles with the long-range third-person crosshair. The server limits the submitted direction to the player's current look cone.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableProjectilePrediction=Trajectory Arc
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableProjectilePrediction.tooltip=Draw a depth-tested 3D trajectory arc for supported vanilla and LOTR projectiles. This client-only preview never moves the fixed crosshair or changes server projectile physics.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableSwimmingDirectionalMovement=Turn the Body While Swimming
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableSwimmingDirectionalMovement.tooltip=Keep camera-relative visual body facing while swimming. Disable to retain vanilla swimming body rotation.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableTargetCrosshair=Crosshair
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableTargetCrosshair.tooltip=Draw a fixed screen-center third-person reticle for the camera-intent ray. The validated target may change behind it, but the reticle never drifts or jitters. Vanilla first-person and disabled-overhaul crosshairs are unchanged.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableTargetLock=Target Lock
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableTargetLock.tooltip=Allow the third-person target-lock key to select a visible server-approved combat enemy from the hostile compass-marker snapshot and steer the local camera toward it. Server reach and line-of-sight validation remain unchanged.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableTargetLockIndicator=Lock Indicator
losttales.config.third_person_camera.enableTargetLockIndicator.tooltip=Draw a restrained gold bracket around the screen center while a target is locked.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.explosionMotionMultiplier=Explosions
losttales.config.third_person_camera.explosionMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales distance-faded camera shake from nearby explosion sounds. Zero disables explosion motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.explosionMotionRadius=Explosion Reach (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.explosionMotionRadius.tooltip=Maximum distance in blocks at which an explosion can shake the third-person camera.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingAngle=Head Turn Angle (Degrees)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingAngle.tooltip=Maximum visible side angle for normal camera-relative head tracking. Reverse camera-facing tracking starts only after the configurable hysteresis and blends in over time.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingHysteresisAngle=Head Turn Margin (Degrees)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingHysteresisAngle.tooltip=Extra camera angle required before entering reverse camera-facing head tracking, and before leaving it again. This prevents rapid shoulder-mode flicker.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingSpeed=Head Turn Speed
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingSpeed.tooltip=Maximum visual head turn speed in degrees per second.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingTransitionSeconds=Head Turn Blend (Seconds)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.headTrackingTransitionSeconds.tooltip=Time used to blend between over-shoulder head tracking and reverse camera-facing tracking. Lower values are more responsive; higher values are softer.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.landingMotionMultiplier=Landing
losttales.config.third_person_camera.landingMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales the landing rebound according to fall speed. Zero disables landing motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.maximumZoomDistance=Farthest Zoom (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.maximumZoomDistance.tooltip=Farthest distance allowed when holding the Lost Tales modifier key and scrolling out.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.minimumZoomDistance=Closest Zoom (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.minimumZoomDistance.tooltip=Closest distance allowed when holding the Lost Tales modifier key and scrolling in.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileAimDistance=Aim Distance (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileAimDistance.tooltip=Maximum raycast distance for the ranged third-person crosshair. This does not change projectile speed, damage, gravity, or entity tracking range.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectoryLineWidth=Arc Width (Pixels)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectoryLineWidth.tooltip=Width of the depth-tested trajectory guide in screen pixels.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectoryOpacity=Arc Opacity
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectoryOpacity.tooltip=Opacity of the client-only trajectory guide.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectoryOriginBlendDistance=Arc Blend Distance (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectoryOriginBlendDistance.tooltip=Distance in blocks over which the guide blends smoothly from the held weapon release point into the exact physical projectile path.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectorySamplesPerTick=Arc Samples per Tick
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectorySamplesPerTick.tooltip=Number of visual curve samples generated between projectile physics ticks. Higher values make the guide smoother without changing prediction physics.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectorySmoothing=Arc Smoothing
losttales.config.third_person_camera.projectileTrajectorySmoothing.tooltip=Tangent strength used to round the visual trajectory between simulated physics points. Zero produces eased straight segments; 0.5 is full Catmull-Rom-style smoothing.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.ridingMotionMultiplier=Riding
losttales.config.third_person_camera.ridingMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales speed-linked mount cadence in the riding camera profile. Zero disables mount-specific motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.shoulderOffsetMultiplier=Shoulder Offset
losttales.config.third_person_camera.shoulderOffsetMultiplier.tooltip=Multiplier for the left/right shoulder offset.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.sprintBodyRotationSpeed=Turn Speed Sprinting
losttales.config.third_person_camera.sprintBodyRotationSpeed.tooltip=Sprinting body turn speed in degrees per second.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.swimmingMotionMultiplier=Swimming
losttales.config.third_person_camera.swimmingMotionMultiplier.tooltip=Scales the slow directional drift used by the swimming camera profile. Zero disables swimming-specific motion.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockHeightFactor=Aim Height
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockHeightFactor.tooltip=Target height fraction used for camera framing and line of sight. 0.5 is body center; higher values favor the upper torso.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockLineOfSightGraceSeconds=Held Out of Sight (Seconds)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockLineOfSightGraceSeconds.tooltip=How long target lock survives a blocked line of sight before releasing.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockPitchSpeed=Turn Speed Up and Down
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockPitchSpeed.tooltip=Maximum vertical target-lock camera turn speed in degrees per second.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockReleaseRange=Release Range (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockReleaseRange.tooltip=Distance in blocks at which an existing target lock is released. Values below the selection range are raised to match it.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockSelectionAngle=Lock Angle (Degrees)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockSelectionAngle.tooltip=Maximum angle in degrees from the camera direction for acquiring or cycling targets.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockSelectionRange=Lock Range (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockSelectionRange.tooltip=Maximum distance in blocks for acquiring and cycling target-lock candidates.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockYawSpeed=Turn Speed Across
losttales.config.third_person_camera.targetLockYawSpeed.tooltip=Maximum horizontal target-lock camera turn speed in degrees per second.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.transitionSpeedMultiplier=Transition Speed
losttales.config.third_person_camera.transitionSpeedMultiplier.tooltip=Multiplier for frame-rate-independent camera transition speeds.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.verticalOffsetMultiplier=Height Offset
losttales.config.third_person_camera.verticalOffsetMultiplier.tooltip=Multiplier for the camera's vertical framing offset.
losttales.config.third_person_camera.zoomStep=Zoom Step (Blocks)
losttales.config.third_person_camera.zoomStep.tooltip=Distance changed by each modifier-key mouse-wheel step.
#   quests, in server/server.cfg
losttales.config.category.quests=Quests
losttales.config.category.quests.tooltip=Quest start rules, prerequisites, rewards, and marker discovery behavior.
losttales.config.quests.allowQuestInteractionStarts=Allow Quest Interaction Starts
losttales.config.quests.allowQuestInteractionStarts.tooltip=Allow right-click entity/block quest giver hooks for quests whose startMode allows interaction starts.
losttales.config.quests.allowQuestItemStarts=Allow Quest Item Starts
losttales.config.quests.allowQuestItemStarts.tooltip=Allow right-click quest starter items with LostTalesQuestId NBT to start quests whose startMode allows item starts.
losttales.config.quests.autoDiscoverNearbyMapMarkers=Auto Discover Nearby Map Markers
losttales.config.quests.autoDiscoverNearbyMapMarkers.tooltip=Automatically discover bundled map markers when a player walks within that marker's unlock radius.
losttales.config.quests.autoPinQuestOnStart=Auto Pin Quest on Start
losttales.config.quests.autoPinQuestOnStart.tooltip=Automatically track a quest on the HUD when it starts, as long as the player is not already tracking it.
losttales.config.quests.autoRevealQuestMarkersOnStart=Auto Reveal Quest Markers on Start
losttales.config.quests.autoRevealQuestMarkersOnStart.tooltip=Automatically reveal marker hints from a quest when that quest starts.
losttales.config.quests.enableQuestPrerequisites=Enable Quest Prerequisites
losttales.config.quests.enableQuestPrerequisites.tooltip=Require optional quest JSON prerequisites before quests can be started.
losttales.config.quests.enableQuestRewards=Enable Quest Rewards
losttales.config.quests.enableQuestRewards.tooltip=Grant optional quest JSON rewards when quests complete naturally or by command.
losttales.config.quests.mapMarkerDiscoveryScanIntervalTicks=Map Marker Discovery Scan Interval Ticks
losttales.config.quests.mapMarkerDiscoveryScanIntervalTicks.tooltip=How often, in ticks, nearby map marker discovery is checked on the server.
#   missives, in server/server.cfg
losttales.config.category.missives=Dynamic Missives
losttales.config.category.missives.tooltip=Missive board refill, notice expiration, and generated timed quest options.
losttales.config.missives.enableDynamicMissiveBoards=Enable Dynamic Missive Boards
losttales.config.missives.enableDynamicMissiveBoards.tooltip=When true, missive board tile entities generate dynamic missive letters on the server.
losttales.config.missives.enableTimedMissives=Enable Timed Missives
losttales.config.missives.enableTimedMissives.tooltip=When true, some generated missives receive a deadline after being accepted.
losttales.config.missives.expireMissiveBoardNotices=Expire Missive Board Notices
losttales.config.missives.expireMissiveBoardNotices.tooltip=When true, old unaccepted notices are removed from missive boards so they can be replaced over time.
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardGenerationIntervalTicks=Missive Board Generation Interval Ticks
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardGenerationIntervalTicks.tooltip=World ticks between a board's ordinary refills; 36000 ticks is 30 real minutes. Every board reads it as it stands.
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMaxAvailable=Missive Board Max Available
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMaxAvailable.tooltip=The most notices a board holds, never fewer than missiveBoardMinAvailable. A board has room for 9; every board reads this as it stands.
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMaxGeneratedPerCycle=Missive Board Max Generated per Cycle
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMaxGeneratedPerCycle.tooltip=Maximum number of new notices generated per refill cycle when space is available.
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMinAvailable=Missive Board Min Available
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMinAvailable.tooltip=Notices a board refills towards: while it holds fewer, each refill posts as many as missiveBoardMaxGeneratedPerCycle allows. A board has room for 9; every board reads this as it stands.
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMinGeneratedPerCycle=Missive Board Min Generated per Cycle
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardMinGeneratedPerCycle.tooltip=Minimum number of new notices generated per refill cycle when space is available.
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardNoticeExpirationDays=Missive Board Notice Expiration Days
losttales.config.missives.missiveBoardNoticeExpirationDays.tooltip=How many in-game days an unaccepted generated board notice remains available before expiring.
losttales.config.missives.timedMissiveChancePercent=Timed Missive Chance Percent
losttales.config.missives.timedMissiveChancePercent.tooltip=Percent chance that a generated missive receives a deadline.
losttales.config.missives.timedMissiveMaxDays=Timed Missive Max Days
losttales.config.missives.timedMissiveMaxDays.tooltip=Maximum accepted-quest deadline length in in-game days for timed missives.
losttales.config.missives.timedMissiveMinDays=Timed Missive Min Days
losttales.config.missives.timedMissiveMinDays.tooltip=Minimum accepted-quest deadline length in in-game days for timed missives.
#   characters, in server/server.cfg
losttales.config.category.characters=Characters
losttales.config.category.characters.tooltip=Which factions a new character may start in, when and how often a player may switch characters, how a character's state is checkpointed, and how long a deleted character can be restored.
losttales.config.characters.allowedStartingFactionIds=Allowed Starting Faction Ids
losttales.config.characters.allowedStartingFactionIds.tooltip=Optional canonical LOTR faction IDs (for example lotr:lothlorien). Empty means all LOTR-playable factions may be offered before race filtering.
losttales.config.characters.characterDeletionRetentionDays=Character Deletion Retention Days
losttales.config.characters.characterDeletionRetentionDays.tooltip=Days a deleted character stays restorable by its player from the roster; after that the server purges it and its saved state at the next start or at the owner's next login.
losttales.config.characters.characterStateCheckpointIntervalSeconds=Character State Checkpoint Interval Seconds
losttales.config.characters.characterStateCheckpointIntervalSeconds.tooltip=Seconds between durable checkpoints of every online active character. Work is spread across server ticks.
losttales.config.characters.characterStateCheckpointPlayersPerTick=Character State Checkpoint Players per Tick
losttales.config.characters.characterStateCheckpointPlayersPerTick.tooltip=Maximum online characters durably checkpointed in one server tick.
losttales.config.characters.characterStateMaxSnapshotBytes=Character State Max Snapshot Bytes
losttales.config.characters.characterStateMaxSnapshotBytes.tooltip=Maximum compressed size of one character-owned player-state snapshot. Oversized snapshots are rejected before switching.
losttales.config.characters.deniedStartingFactionIds=Denied Starting Faction Ids
losttales.config.characters.deniedStartingFactionIds.tooltip=Canonical LOTR faction IDs excluded from character creation. Deny entries override allow entries.
losttales.config.characters.switchCombatGraceSeconds=Switch Combat Grace Seconds
losttales.config.characters.switchCombatGraceSeconds.tooltip=Reject switching for this many seconds after incoming or outgoing combat evidence.
losttales.config.characters.switchCooldownDecaySeconds=Switch Cooldown Decay Seconds
losttales.config.characters.switchCooldownDecaySeconds.tooltip=Inactivity required to decay each current cooldown stage. Higher stages should use longer values.
losttales.config.characters.switchCooldownSeconds=Switch Cooldown Seconds
losttales.config.characters.switchCooldownSeconds.tooltip=Escalating server-authoritative cooldown stages in seconds. The default is 1m, 3m, 5m, 15m, 30m, 60m.
losttales.config.characters.switchStableGroundTicks=Switch Stable Ground Ticks
losttales.config.characters.switchStableGroundTicks.tooltip=Number of consecutive safe grounded ticks required before switching.
losttales.config.characters.switchTeleportDistancePerTick=Switch Teleport Distance per Tick
losttales.config.characters.switchTeleportDistancePerTick.tooltip=Movement farther than this many blocks in one tick is treated as teleportation.
losttales.config.characters.switchTeleportGraceSeconds=Switch Teleport Grace Seconds
losttales.config.characters.switchTeleportGraceSeconds.tooltip=Reject switching for this many seconds after teleport, respawn, or dimension-transition evidence.
#   combat_markers, in server/server.cfg
losttales.config.category.combatMarkers=Combat Markers
losttales.config.category.combatMarkers.tooltip=Server-authoritative range, update cadence, disengagement grace, and diagnostics for temporary enemy markers.
losttales.config.combat_markers.debugLogging=Debug Logging
losttales.config.combat_markers.debugLogging.tooltip=Log changed combat marker snapshots. Disabled by default to avoid log spam.
losttales.config.combat_markers.disengagementGraceTicks=Disengagement Grace Ticks
losttales.config.combat_markers.disengagementGraceTicks.tooltip=Ticks that an exact player/entity combat relationship may remain visible after direct evidence disappears.
losttales.config.combat_markers.shareWithFellowship=Share with Fellowship
losttales.config.combat_markers.shareWithFellowship.tooltip=Share server-approved active-combat enemy markers with authorized nearby members of the same role-playing fellowship.
losttales.config.combat_markers.trackingRadius=Tracking Radius
losttales.config.combat_markers.trackingRadius.tooltip=Server-authoritative maximum range in blocks for player-specific combat marker tracking.
losttales.config.combat_markers.updateIntervalTicks=Update Interval Ticks
losttales.config.combat_markers.updateIntervalTicks.tooltip=Server ticks between combat-state scans. Snapshots are sent only when their contents change.
#   fellowship, in server/server.cfg
losttales.config.category.fellowship=Fellowships
losttales.config.category.fellowship.tooltip=How often member status and positions are sent, and shared quest credit. How many members a fellowship may have is LOTR's setting.
losttales.config.fellowship.enableSharedQuestProgress=Enable Shared Quest Progress
losttales.config.fellowship.enableSharedQuestProgress.tooltip=Allow authoritative kill and destination-arrival events to advance matching Lost Tales objectives for eligible nearby fellowship members. Gathering, crafting, hand-ins, completion, and rewards remain individual.
losttales.config.fellowship.sharedQuestRadius=Shared Quest Radius
losttales.config.fellowship.sharedQuestRadius.tooltip=Maximum block distance for conservative fellowship-shared kill and travel objective progress. Members must be online, alive, in the same dimension, using the fellowship character, and independently possess the matching quest.
losttales.config.fellowship.statusHeartbeatTicks=Status Heartbeat Ticks
losttales.config.fellowship.statusHeartbeatTicks.tooltip=Maximum server ticks between unchanged fellowship status snapshots for online fellowship members.
losttales.config.fellowship.statusUpdateIntervalTicks=Status Update Interval Ticks
losttales.config.fellowship.statusUpdateIntervalTicks.tooltip=Server ticks between fellowship health and availability checks. Packets are sent only when state changes or a heartbeat is due.
losttales.config.fellowship.trackingHeartbeatTicks=Tracking Heartbeat Ticks
losttales.config.fellowship.trackingHeartbeatTicks.tooltip=Maximum server ticks between unchanged fellowship tracking snapshots for online fellowship members.
losttales.config.fellowship.trackingUpdateIntervalTicks=Tracking Update Interval Ticks
losttales.config.fellowship.trackingUpdateIntervalTicks.tooltip=Server ticks between authorized fellowship position checks. Coordinates are quantized and packets are sent only when state changes or a heartbeat is due.
#   chat, in server/server.cfg
losttales.config.category.chat=Chat Channels
losttales.config.category.chat.tooltip=Server-side chat: proximity routing, typing relay and the audit log.
losttales.config.chat.auditLog=Audit Log
losttales.config.chat.auditLog.tooltip=Server only: append every accepted chat message, edit, and deletion - private whispers included - as JSON lines under logs/losttales-chat/, one file per UTC day, for moderation. Off by default; tell your players before turning it on.
losttales.config.chat.auditRetentionDays=Audit Retention Days
losttales.config.chat.auditRetentionDays.tooltip=Days of chat audit files kept; files older than this are deleted when the server starts and as the day rolls over.
losttales.config.chat.historyPerChannel=History per Channel
losttales.config.chat.historyPerChannel.tooltip=Server only: the most messages of each channel the history keeps, live and in the save; the oldest go first. A joining player is replayed at most 100 of a channel and 400 in all of them.
losttales.config.chat.historyPersisted=History Persisted
losttales.config.chat.historyPersisted.tooltip=Server only: keep the recent chat history in the world save, so a player who rejoins after a restart is still shown the conversation they missed. Off keeps it in memory for the server's run alone.
losttales.config.chat.profanityWords=Profanity Words
losttales.config.chat.profanityWords.tooltip=Words added to the chat's profanity list beside the ones the mod bundles, one per line as word=replacement, both a run of letters: the word, matched whole with stretched letters and the common endings, and the silly word that stands in for it. Sent to every client with its chat access, refused in a character's name, and applied to what the Discord bridge posts when discord.profanityFilter says so. An entry naming a bundled word replaces its stand-in.
losttales.config.chat.proximityRadius=Proximity Radius
losttales.config.chat.proximityRadius.tooltip=Server-authoritative maximum distance in blocks for Proximity chat recipients.
losttales.config.chat.serverAddress=Server Address
losttales.config.chat.serverAddress.tooltip=Server only: the address players join this server by (play.example.org), shown to every player in the Server's status line in the member lists and in the topic of every linked Discord channel. Empty shows none; the server never reads an address off the machine, since its own may be a private one.
losttales.config.chat.typingIndicators=Typing Indicators
losttales.config.chat.typingIndicators.tooltip=Relay who is typing into a channel to the players who would read the message; off drops every typing notice on the server.
losttales.config.chat.welcomeLines=Welcome Lines
losttales.config.chat.welcomeLines.tooltip=Server only: what a new player is greeted with the first time they join this world, as Server lines in OOC Chat that wait there unread: the rules, a Discord invite, anything. One line each, at most 8 lines of 1,024 characters; a web address becomes a link. Empty greets nobody.
