#   Page help
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.everyone=Everyone online reads %s.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.proximity=Only those near you read %s, in your world.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.faction=Everyone of your faction reads %s.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.fellowship=The fellowship's members read %s, and nobody else.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.self=Only you read %s: the commands you type, their answers and what the game tells you.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.console=%s records what the server does, from commands run to settings changed, for those allowed to read it. You can talk in it.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.operators=Only those the server lets in read %s.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.whisper=Only you and %s read this conversation.
gui.losttales.help.chat.readers.npc=%s is someone of the world. Your answers stay on your computer.
gui.losttales.help.chat.speaking.played=You speak in character, as the character you play.
gui.losttales.help.chat.speaking.identity=You speak in character, as the identity on the bar's second button.
gui.losttales.help.chat.speaking.account=You speak out of character, as your account.
gui.losttales.help.chat.1=Type in the bar and press Return to send. Shift+Return starts a new paragraph.
gui.losttales.help.chat.2=Point at a message for its actions. Right-click a message or a name for more, and click a name to open that person's card.
gui.losttales.help.chat.3=Type : for emoji, @ to mention someone, # for a channel, and [i:, [m: or [q: to share an item, a place or a quest. /me tells what your character does.
gui.losttales.help.chat.4=The bell and the bubble on the tool strip hold this conversation's own settings, which lines chime and which reach the chat feed; so do the three dots on its tab. The cog opens Chat Settings, the same for every conversation.
gui.losttales.help.page.journal.1=Your quests, by where they stand. Pick one in the list to read it.
gui.losttales.help.page.journal.2=Track a quest to follow it on the HUD and the map. Share it in the chat so your fellowship can join.
gui.losttales.help.page.fellowship.1=The fellowships of the character you play, and the invitations waiting for you or sent by them. Pick a fellowship's row to act on it; the HUD, the compass and shared quest credit follow the one you travel with.
gui.losttales.help.page.fellowship.2=The leader and the guides invite by name in the bar and set the icon and the rules on harm; the leader alone decides whether members show on the map, names the fellowship, makes guides and hands on the lead. Each fellowship has a conversation of its own.
gui.losttales.help.page.map.1=Middle-earth as far as you have seen it. Drag to move the map, turn the wheel to zoom, and drag with the right button to turn and lean it.
gui.losttales.help.page.map.2=Click a waypoint to travel there. Click the bare map to set where the fellowship you travel with gathers. The legend shows and hides each kind of marker.
gui.losttales.help.page.characters.1=Your characters. Pick one in the roster to read its profile, and Play as to switch to it.
gui.losttales.help.page.characters.2=Drag the figure to turn it. Edit Profile says who your character is; others read it on your card.
gui.losttales.help.page.motion_lab.1=Every motion of the mod's screens and HUD. Pick one, change its values and watch the sample.
gui.losttales.help.page.motion_lab.2=Save keeps the motions you tuned on your computer. Copy gives a motion's text for the mod's own files.
gui.losttales.help.page.new_page.1=Every page you can open, by its kind. Pick one and this tab becomes it. A page open already opens again, as a copy with a view of its own.
gui.losttales.help.page.new_page.2=Right-click a kind's name to reach all its pages at once. Words in the search show the pages as one list.
gui.losttales.help.page.new_page.3=The arrow keys walk the pages: up and down from one kind into the next, left and right round the kinds. Enter opens the page lit.
gui.losttales.help.page.client_settings.1=Every setting with no page of its own: the camera, the screens and the look of bodies. The HUD's are on the HUD Placement page.
gui.losttales.help.page.client_settings.2=A setting is saved the moment you change it. A click steps it on, a right-click steps it back.
gui.losttales.help.page.inbox.1=What is addressed to you: fellowship invitations to the character you play, lines that mention you, messages forwarded to you in a whisper, and the quest news of this session.
gui.losttales.help.page.inbox.2=A click goes where a row names: the line in its conversation, the invitation on the Fellowships page, the quest in the journal. The inbox button on every conversation's tool strip counts what waits: invitations not yet answered, mentions and forwards not yet read, quest news not yet seen here.
gui.losttales.help.page.hud_placement.1=The whole screen in small. At the left each panel of the HUD stands as a box with its name: drag it where it should stand. At the right the preview shows the screen as it will look while you play.
gui.losttales.help.page.hud_placement.2=A box pulls to the middle of the screen as it nears it. Default Place puts the panel picked back where it first stood; Panel Layout puts every panel in its place at once. The switches show the HUD and each panel; HUD Settings, behind the cog, hold each panel's place as numbers and the compass's own settings.
gui.losttales.help.page.server_settings.1=The server's own settings, for those it lets change them.
gui.losttales.help.page.server_settings.2=Your changes wait in honey until you save them. Discard puts them back; Refresh asks the server again.
gui.losttales.help.page.waystone.1=This waystone's name, its marker and who may use it.
gui.losttales.help.page.waystone.2=Destinations opens the map to pick where to travel. Save sends your changes, and the server checks each.
gui.losttales.help.page.missive_board.1=The notices pinned to this board. Accept one to take its missive, or take its letter with you.
gui.losttales.help.page.missive_board.2=Pin Letter puts a letter you carry up on the board for others.
gui.losttales.help.page.missive_letter.1=A missive in your hands. Accept takes its task; the letter says how long you have.
